  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\nPattern turns busier in the wake of the second cold front coming \nthrough tonight, and a closed upper low dropping into the southern \nGreat Lakes. Line of showers with the front tonight, then a \ntransition to cold air advection showers with low level flows off of \nLake Erie Friday through Saturday night. Showers in the wake of the \nfront will primarily involve the lake effect areas with near surface \nf-gen occurring downstream of non-zero values of 0-2km CAPE over \nLake Erie. Moderate rain showers for short periods of time will not \nbe out of the question as a result. 850mb temperatures below zero \nwill translate to upper 40s away from the lakeshore Saturday and \nlower 50s along the lakeshore, but still far too warm for any frozen \nprecipitation in the forecast. Upper low and favorable low level \nflows off the lake will exit Sunday as high pressure builds over the \nTennessee Valley.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \nUpper pattern more zonal through early next week, so this will keep \nthe warming trend on the gradual side without any significant \nmeridional swings to the upper level pattern. Dry weather returns to \nthe fold with 60s back in the forecast for Monday and Tuesday. \nLooking at another brief and modest cool down into the end of next \nweek.",
